codex
A first candidate—plain planted random 3-colorable graphs—fails the spirit of H: a simple DSATUR backtracker solves 180-vertex samples in milliseconds, even though naive guessing and the three mandated attacks look good. I’m discarding that construction.

I’m now testing a harder specialization that is still exactly the paper’s \(S=(1,1,\ldots)\) coloring definition: graph-color encodings of planted partial Latin-square completion. The anchor clique and row/column cliques make verification just edge scanning, while the planted completion is sampled before clues. I’m measuring against a direct completion solver before committing.
